<DocsLayout title="Getting started" description="Install etmc, add a relay and start playing.">
  <p>Everyone who plays needs etmc installed, whether they're hosting or joining.</p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Install <a href="https://fabricmc.net/">Fabric</a>, <a href="https://neoforged.net/">NeoForge</a> or
      <a href="https://files.minecraftforge.net/">Forge</a>.</li>
    <li>Download the etmc jar for your loader and Minecraft version from
      <a href="https://github.com/L5Z12/etmc/releases">Releases</a>.</li>
    <li>Put it in your <code>mods</code> folder. On Fabric, add
      <a href="https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api">Fabric API</a> too.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Add a relay</h2>
  <p>
    A relay helps players find each other, and carries the game when they can't connect directly. Any EasyTier node
    works, so you can pick a free one from this <a href="https://ruixuan.online/uptime/easytier">list of public
    nodes</a> or run your own.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Press <kbd>G</kbd>, click <strong>etmc</strong> in the pause menu or on the Multiplayer screen, or run
      <code>/etmc menu</code>.</li>
    <li>Open <strong>Settings</strong> and add your relay, such as <code>tcp://my.relay:11010</code>.
      <strong>Find a relay</strong> opens the list of public nodes. If you skip this, etmc asks for one when you
      host.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>If you're joining with an invite link, you can skip this step, because the link includes the relay.</p>
  <div class="note">Public nodes are shared with strangers. Anyone using the same network name and secret lands on
    the same network, so keep the random ones etmc gives you.</div>

  <h2>Play</h2>
  <p>Next, <a href="/docs/hosting">host a world</a> or <a href="/docs/joining">join one</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
